  <!-- PANELS VS TILES -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f1f5f9;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Are bathroom wall panels better than tiles?</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">Panels are cheaper, quicker and have no grout to keep clean. Tiles win on choice and on resale appeal in higher value homes. Here is the honest comparison.</p>

      <div class="cmp-wrap">
        <table class="cmp-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">What matters</th>
              <th scope="col">Wall panels</th>
              <th scope="col">Tiles</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Cost of the wall finish</th>
              <td data-label="Wall panels"><span class="cmp-win">40 to 60 percent less</span></td>
              <td data-label="Tiles">Higher, plus a tiler's day rate on top</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Time to fit</th>
              <td data-label="Wall panels"><span class="cmp-win">Hours</span></td>
              <td data-label="Tiles">3 to 5 days for a full bathroom</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Grout to clean and reseal</th>
              <td data-label="Wall panels"><span class="cmp-win">None</span></td>
              <td data-label="Tiles">Yes, and it darkens over time</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Trades needed</th>
              <td data-label="Wall panels"><span class="cmp-win">One team, one visit</span></td>
              <td data-label="Tiles">A separate tiler you book yourself</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Choice of pattern and texture</th>
              <td data-label="Wall panels">Limited to the panel ranges</td>
              <td data-label="Tiles"><span class="cmp-win">Almost unlimited</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Appeal to a buyer on resale</th>
              <td data-label="Wall panels">Fine in most homes</td>
              <td data-label="Tiles"><span class="cmp-win">Stronger in higher value homes</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Repairing damage later</th>
              <td data-label="Wall panels">Whole panel usually replaced</td>
              <td data-label="Tiles"><span class="cmp-win">Single tiles can be swapped</span></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="pf-alert" style="margin-top:1.75rem;">
        <strong>Which one we would tell you to pick</strong>
        <p>For a working family bathroom, panels almost always make more sense. The money saved on the wall finish buys a better suite. For a period property, or a house at the top of its street's price range, tiles are usually worth the extra and the extra trade. We will tell you which way we would go in your room at the free survey, even when that means telling you to spend more elsewhere.</p>
