  <!-- BATH TO SHOWER -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f8fafc;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>How much does it cost to replace a bath with a shower?</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">A bath to shower conversion in Liverpool starts at £2,200 and takes 2 to 3 days. It is the single job we are asked for most often.</p>

      <div class="pf-card pf-card-navy" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <h3>What the job actually involves</h3>
        <p>The bath comes out first. The old taps and waste are capped or adapted, and this is usually where problems show up. A bath that has been in for twenty years often hides a rotten floorboard or a waste joint that has been weeping. We check for that before anything new goes in and we tell you what we find.</p>
        <p>The tray is set and levelled, the valve is fitted and the walls behind the shower are panelled. Then the enclosure goes on and the whole thing is tested. If getting in and out of a bath is the reason for the job, ask about a low level tray. It makes the step in much smaller and costs no more to fit.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="pf-card pf-card-orange" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <h3>Check your water system before you buy a shower</h3>
        <p>This is the thing that catches people out. A shower that is wrong for your water system will dribble no matter how good it is. A combi boiler, a vented cylinder and an unvented cylinder all behave differently. We check what you have at the survey and match the valve to it. If you have already bought a shower, bring it out and we will tell you honestly whether it will work.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

