      <h2>How does a bathroom installation work?</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">Six stages from the first visit to the day we hand the room back.</p>
      <div class="pf-steps" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <div class="pf-step"><div class="pf-step-num">1</div><div><strong>Free survey</strong><p>We come out, measure the room and check where the existing pipes and waste run. That last part matters more than people expect, because moving a waste is what turns a simple job into an expensive one. The survey takes about 45 minutes and costs nothing.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-step"><div class="pf-step-num">2</div><div><strong>Fixed price quote</strong><p>You get the full spec written down with a fixed price. What is included is listed and so is what is not. If you want to change the suite or drop something to hit a budget, we adjust it before you commit.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-step"><div class="pf-step-num">3</div><div><strong>Strip out and disposal</strong><p>The old bathroom comes out and leaves with us. You do not need a skip and you do not need a permit for one.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-step"><div class="pf-step-num">4</div><div><strong>First fix plumbing</strong><p>New supply and waste pipework goes in and gets clipped properly. If we find damp, rot or a failed waste under the old suite, we show you and price the fix before carrying on. Nothing gets covered up.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-step"><div class="pf-step-num">5</div><div><strong>Panels and second fix</strong><p>Wall panels go up. Then the bath or enclosure, the toilet, the basin and the vanity are fitted and plumbed in. Taps and valves on, everything connected.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-step"><div class="pf-step-num">6</div><div><strong>Test and handover</strong><p>Every joint tested under pressure. Silicone finished properly. The room cleaned before we leave, not left for you to do.</p></div></div>
